{"content":[{"c":["FISH GATE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Gate probably located in the north wall of the city of Jerusalem. The Fish Gate was built in David’s time and later formed part of Manasseh’s fortifications (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.33.14","r":"2Chr.33.14","rawR":"2Chr.33.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.33.14","value":"2Chr.33.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 33:14"},"). After the Babylonian exile, it was restored under Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.3","r":"Neh.3.3","rawR":"Neh.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.3","value":"Neh.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.39","r":"Neh.12.39","rawR":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.39","value":"Neh.12.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:39"},"); it is mentioned along with the Mishneh or Second Quarter (",{"href":"?bref=Zeph.1.10","r":"Zeph.1.10","rawR":"Zeph.1.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zeph.1.10","value":"Zeph.1.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zep 1:10"},"). The gate was probably so named either because fish were brought into the city from the north, or because it was located near the city’s fish market."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"FishGate","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Chr 33:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.33.14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.33.14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.33.14"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.3","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.3","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.3"},{"anchorText":"12:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.39","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.39","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.39"},{"anchorText":"Zep 1:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zeph.1.10","rawQueryValue":"Zeph.1.10","sourceRefExact":"Zeph.1.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"df708be980846de41a7cb5fbeeab5aba671ae559d849648f2c3956d4db398b90","sourceItemName":"FishGate","sourceItemOrder":45,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"FishGate","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Fish Gate","title":"Fish Gate","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}